# Fixture, not repo hygiene. `build/` and `excluded/` exist so the collector
# is tested against a real .gitignore; `.oracleignore` then rescues
# `!build/keep.md` and `!excluded/reincluded/kept.md`. Those two files are
# force-tracked (`git add -f`). Do not "fix" this list — without it the
# ignore-semantics golden tests are testing nothing.
build/
excluded/
